# canonical-golden.hex — JVM-DERIVED golden canonical-bytes vector (lowercase hex) for the
# domain-registry signed-export signature path. This is the EXTERNAL, INDEPENDENT anchor that
# tests/domain-registry/test-domain-reconcile-verify.sh Case 0 compares the bash
# domain_canonical_bytes (specs/usr/lib/snapdragon/domain-verify.sh) output against, so a FUTURE
# self-consistent-but-wrong edit to the bash reconstruction is caught (the ACCEPT/REJECT cases
# alone cannot catch that — they sign whatever domain_canonical_bytes emits and verify the same).
#
# DERIVATION ROUTE: JVM. Produced by tests/domain-registry/Golden.java, a single-file Java program
# that copies the byte-layout of canonicalBytes VERBATIM from the authoritative admin-bff signer
#   snapdragon-admin-bff-api:
#   src/main/java/systems/snapdragon/adminbff/domainregistry/DomainRegistryExportService.java
#   static byte[] canonicalBytes(DomainExportBody)   (the merged #118 version on origin/main)
# Cross-checked byte-for-byte against an independent python3 byte-assembly of the documented layout.
#
# FIXTURE (must match Case 0 / canon_ref() in the test EXACTLY):
#   node       = mkey:abc
#   generation = 7
#   one DomainEntry: clusterDomain=acme.test  brand=acme  org=Acme-Inc  caRef=generate
#                    nsPrefix=acme  casdoorOrg=acme-org  meshTag=tag:acme
#                    caProvisioned=false  appsetRegistered=false  generation=7
#
# DECODED canonical bytes (159 bytes, \t = TAB, \n = LF, no trailing byte after the final \n):
#   v1-domain\n
#   node=mkey:abc\n
#   generation=7\n
#   dom=acme.test\tbrand=acme\torg=Acme-Inc\tca=generate\tns=acme\tcasdoor=acme-org\tmesh=tag:acme\tca_prov=false\tappset=false\tgen=7\n
#
# REGENERATE (ONLY if DomainRegistryExportService.canonicalBytes changes):
#   java tests/domain-registry/Golden.java   # prints the single hex line below
# NOT wired into CI (generator CI is GitLab and ships no JDK) — this is a committed static vector;
# Golden.java is a manual regen tool. If this contract changes, update domain-verify.sh + this
# golden together and re-run the offline test.

